    "teach_2": {
      "id": "teach_2",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Now the exam upgrades the ask: from x + 1/x, find x^2 + 1/x^2.\n\nSquare the given:\n\n(x + 1/x)^2 = x^2 + 2 × x × 1/x + 1/x^2\n\nThe middle term collapses: 2 × x × 1/x = 2.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_2_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_2_step": {
      "id": "teach_2_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "So with x + 1/x = 6:\n\n36 = x^2 + 1/x^2 + 2\nx^2 + 1/x^2 = 34\n\nThe recipe: square the given, subtract 2. That 2 is the price of squaring.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_2"
        }
      ]
    },
