    "teach_3": {
      "id": "teach_3",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The book's classic: x + 1/x = 17/4. Find x − 1/x.\n\nFirst get the squares:\n\nx^2 + 1/x^2 = (17/4)^2 − 2 = 289/16 − 32/16 = 257/16",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_3_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_3_step": {
      "id": "teach_3_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Now subtract 2 again to flip the middle sign:\n\n(x − 1/x)^2 = 257/16 − 2 = 257/16 − 32/16 = 225/16\n\nTake the root:\n\nx − 1/x = 15/4\n\nTwo steps of −2: one to square up, one to flip to minus.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_3"
        }
      ]
    },
