    "teach_4": {
      "id": "teach_4",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Different shape now — chained ratios.\n\na/b = 4/15 and b/c = 5/16. Find a/c.\n\nThe b is a bridge. Multiply the ratios and the bridge cancels:\n\na/b × b/c = a/c",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_4_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_4_step": {
      "id": "teach_4_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Compute:\n\na/c = 4/15 × 5/16 = 20/240 = 1/12\n\nOne multiplication, no algebra.\n\nThe exam then asks things like (c^2 − a^2)/(c^2 + a^2) — which we handle next with the same idea.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_4"
        }
      ]
    },
