    "teach_5": {
      "id": "teach_5",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Given a ratio, you can value any matching expression.\n\nc/a = 4/3. Find (c^2 − a^2)/(c^2 + a^2).\n\nDivide every term by a^2:\n\n= (c^2/a^2 − 1)/(c^2/a^2 + 1)",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_5_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_5_step": {
      "id": "teach_5_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Now substitute (c/a)^2 = 16/9:\n\n= (16/9 − 1)/(16/9 + 1)\n= (7/9)/(25/9)\n= 7/25\n\nTrick summary: square the ratio, divide the expression through, substitute.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_5"
        }
      ]
    },
