    "teach_6": {
      "id": "teach_6",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "One elegant trick to finish the algebra section.\n\nGiven a + b = 2c, find a/(a − c) + c/(b − c).\n\nFrom a + b = 2c, slide terms:\n\nb − c = c − a = −(a − c)",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_6_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_6_step": {
      "id": "teach_6_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "So the second denominator is the flip of the first:\n\na/(a − c) + c/(b − c)\n= a/(a − c) − c/(a − c)\n= (a − c)/(a − c)\n= 1\n\nThe whole expression collapses to 1 — no values needed.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_6"
        }
      ]
    },
